From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: identify zero-link MLD control sockets
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A hostapd AP MLD control endpoint survives removal of its last active
link while retained BSSes still reference the MLD. GET_CONFIG and STATUS
then return FAIL because there is no first BSS to receive the command.
After TERMINATING resets a local AP connection to its bare name, radio
removal mistakes this endpoint for an unresolved local BSS:

  wlan0: unresolved local socket wlan0.1, abort radio removal

When both identity queries explicitly fail, probe with LINKID 0 PING.
Only the MLD control handler accepts the LINKID prefix and returns
NO LINKS ACTIVE when no first BSS exists; hostapd sends that reply as
16 bytes, LF included and without a NUL, and the command transport
strips the trailing LF. Ordinary BSS sockets return UNKNOWN COMMAND.
Require the exact reply and an unchanged socket inode before marking the
endpoint nonBss. Keep it unresolved so it cannot be adopted as an AP or
become a REMOVE target. Do not infer endpoint type from a bare pathname,
FAIL, or missing BSS fields alone. Trace the outcome either way, so a
FAIL/FAIL socket that is not an MLD endpoint is visible in the log
before the removal preflight aborts on it.

Leave the unknown-local-BSS and radio-local first-BSS owner guards
unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_sock.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_sock.c b/src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_sock.c
index 9cf9af15cf1e..a0218a234610 100644
--- a/src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_sock.c
+++ b/src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_sock.c
@@ -138,12 +138,36 @@ swl_rc_ne wld_hostapd_resolveSock(const char* dir, const char* name, wld_hostapd
     char value[128] = {0};
     memset(reply, 0, sizeof(reply));
     swl_rc_ne rc = wld_wpaCtrl_queryToSock(dir, name, "GET_CONFIG", reply, sizeof(reply));
+    bool configFailed = swl_rc_isOk(rc) && swl_str_matches(reply, "FAIL");
     bool hasBssid = swl_rc_isOk(rc) && s_value(reply, "bssid", value, sizeof(value)) &&
                     swl_typeMacBin_fromChar(&pSock->bssid, value) && !swl_mac_binIsNull(&pSock->bssid);
     /* STATUS can still identify a local candidate if GET_CONFIG timed out. */
     memset(reply, 0, sizeof(reply));
     rc = wld_wpaCtrl_queryToSock(dir, name, "STATUS", reply, sizeof(reply));
     ASSERTI_TRUE(swl_rc_isOk(rc), SWL_RC_ERROR, ME, "STATUS unavailable: %s", name);
+    if(configFailed && swl_str_matches(reply, "FAIL")) {
+        /*
+         * An AP MLD control endpoint survives its last active link. Bare
+         * GET_CONFIG/STATUS then return FAIL, so neither can identify a
+         * redirect. Only the MLD handler understands LINKID and replies
+         * "NO LINKS ACTIVE\n" (16 bytes, LF included, no NUL) when it has
+         * no first BSS; the command transport strips that trailing LF.
+         * A BSS socket returns UNKNOWN COMMAND instead; FAIL alone must
+         * never exempt a socket.
+         */
+        memset(reply, 0, sizeof(reply));
+        rc = wld_wpaCtrl_queryToSock(dir, name, "LINKID 0 PING", reply, sizeof(reply));
+        bool sameInode = (pSock->inode == s_inode(dir, name));
+        pSock->nonBss = swl_rc_isOk(rc) && swl_str_matches(reply, "NO LINKS ACTIVE") && sameInode;
+        if(pSock->nonBss) {
+            SAH_TRACEZ_INFO(ME, "zero-link MLD endpoint %s", name);
+        } else {
+            SAH_TRACEZ_WARNING(ME, "%s: FAIL/FAIL socket is not an MLD endpoint (rc %d, reply '%s'%s)",
+                               name, rc, reply, sameInode ? "" : ", socket replaced");
+        }
+        /* A confirmed MLD endpoint still has no resolved BSS identity. */
+        return SWL_RC_ERROR;
+    }
     pSock->enabled = s_value(reply, "state", value, sizeof(value)) && swl_str_matches(value, "ENABLED");
     s_value(reply, "phy", pSock->phy, sizeof(pSock->phy));
     pSock->hasBand = s_value(reply, "freq", value, sizeof(value)) && (atoi(value) > 0) &&
